       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You've confirmed it, but a single 50 mg dose of amlodipine has no therapeutic use. It's well above the 10 mg daily maximum, and I can't see a scenario where giving it to this patient would be safe. You also haven't given a clinical rationale.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** Tell me 2.5, 5, or 10 mg once daily and I'll enter it.\n- **Help you escalate.** If you think the patient needs more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, a better option is usually to add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. I can enter that, or you can discuss it with your attending or pharmacy.\n- **Use the pharmacy and attending route.** If there's a real reason for a non-standard dose, it should be ordered with attending sign-off and pharmacist review, not entered through me.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
      }
     ],
